{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To clarify for them by the word of HaShem.</b> 'לפרש' implies clarifying everything — for they did not know whether he was liable to stoning, from a kal vachomer from one who curses his father and mother, concerning whom it is written 'אביו ואמו קלל' — 'his father and mother he cursed,' and his death is in it [i.e., indicated]. Or perhaps it is not [merely] logical that he should be punished by the death penalty of the court, so that he would have no atonement, because his punishment is great? As we say regarding one who passes his son or daughter through fire: 'איש כי יתן מזרעו' — and we derive: 'מזרעו' and not all his seed; from here they said: one who passes all his seed is exempt. And this 'exempt' does not mean literally exempt, for if so we would find a sinner who profits; rather it means they exempt him from the death penalty of the court, so that he not be atoned by that. Therefore it needed to say 'to clarify for them by the word of HaShem.' But regarding the wood-gatherer, they knew for certain that he was liable to the death penalty, as it is said 'מחלליה מות יומת' — but they did not know by which death he is executed: whether by strangulation, since any unspecified death penalty mentioned in the Torah is nothing but strangulation; or we derive the punishment of desecration from idolatry. Therefore it does not say regarding him 'לפרש,' but rather 'כי לא פורש מה יעשה לו.' And there is a difficulty here and there according to Rabbi Yehudah, who says he is not executed until they inform him by which death he is executed — if so, how were these [men] liable? Perhaps they warned them with all four death penalties of the court, and they accepted [warning] upon themselves for all of them. Yet this is difficult according to the one who says that a doubtful warning is not called warning, for in each and every death penalty it constitutes a doubtful warning. And it is far-fetched that there would be among them so many witnesses that they warned them with all of them together. And perhaps this is possible, since here it is written 'וסמכו השמעים' — and it is not written 'the witnesses,' and likewise regarding the wood-gatherer it is written 'ויהיו בני ישראל במדבר וימצאו איש מקושש' — implying that many were there. And further, one may say: they were associates (חברים), and they held that an associate does not require warning. תן לחכם ויחכם עוד."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:31.984251716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}